3 STAE Uppland
3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU Professor i Uppsala
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Petrus "Per" Ekerman''' was a Swedish professor in the University of Uppsala. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His parents were''' Maria Löfgren and Paul Enerman, the vicar of West Eneby. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1727, Ekerman''' was appointed as a Docent in Philosophy at the University of Uppsala, the following year as an assistant professor of philosophy, or Adjunct and in 1729 as Secretary of the University. Ekerman was appointed 
2 CONC professor of poetry and eloquence in 1737 and remained in office until his retirement in 1779.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1745, Ekerman''' supervised [https://www.geni.com/people/Christopher-T%C3%A4rnstr%C3%B6m/6000000079567491028 '''Christopher Tärnström''']'s doctoral dissertation [http://urn.fi/URN:NBN:fi-fd2010-00003239 '''Dissertatio Acade
2 CONC mica de Alandia Maris Baltici Insula'''], where the two scholars made observations of the Åland Islands, including its birdlife.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ekerman remains the''' most productive supervisor of doctoral dissertations in Sweden. In total, he supervised 615 theses. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ekerman and Anna Törner''', the daughter of a professor, married in 1730. They had at least four children, two of whom died less than a year old. The third daughter, Eva Maria Ekerman (b. 1733, 1803), married in 1764 with Profe
2 CONC ssor Carl Aurivillius (b. 1717, c. 1786) and was the daughter of Eva Maria Aurivillius (b. 1758, 1844).
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
