1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irina_Bj%C3%B6rklund '''Irina Björklund'''] (born 7 February 1973) is a Finnish actress and singer.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Acting'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Björklund studied''' in the Theatre Academy of Finland from 1993 to 1996. She left the school when Svenska Teatern (Swedish theatre in Helsinki) hired her.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She has acted''' in several movies and television series. Her well-known movies include Rukajärven tie (int. Ambush), Levottomat (int. Restless), Minä ja Morrison (int. Me and Morrison), and Vieraalla Maalla (int. Land of Love)
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1999, Björklund''' was awarded the Jussi Award for Best Leading Actress for her role as Milla in the movie Minä ja Morrison. Her breakthrough came in the movie Rukajärven tie, in which she played Lotta Kaarina Vainikainen. S
2 CONC he was awarded the Shooting Star prize in the Berlin Film Festival in 2004.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In September 2010''', Björklund's career advanced when she landed a minor role in The American] alongside George Clooney. She played the role of Clooney's lover, Ingrid.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Music'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Björklund made a duet''' with Samuli Edelmann titled "Niin kaunis on maa". In 2011, she released her own music album in French with lyrics by Björklund and music by American Peter Fox. The album called Chanson d'automne did wel
2 CONC l in the Finnish Albums Chart reaching #21. In 2014, she released another French-language album, La vie est une fête with an even higher charting in Finland reaching #6.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Other'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Björklund moved to''' the Los Angeles in 1999 with husband and Finnish actor Peter Franzén,where they lived until 2013, when they moved to France. The couple has a son, born in September 2007.
